  [1mWhen localStorage is unavailable at all[0m, the factory falls back to an in-memory store. This matters more than it
  sounds: some browsers throw a [38;5;153mSecurityError[39m on merely [3maccessing[0m [38;5;153mwindow.localStorage[39m (a page embedded in an iframe with
  third-party storage blocked), so the wiring has to guard property access, not just [38;5;153msetItem[39m. With the fallback,
  preferences work normally for the life of the page and simply don't survive it, and the login form never knows the
  difference.

  [1mCorrupt data always degrades to defaults, never to an exception.[0m Unparseable JSON, a stored value that isn't an
  object, [38;5;153mnull[39m, or an unrecognised [38;5;153mversion[39m all load as all-defaults. A single field failing its validator falls back to
  just that field's default, as covered in section 1.

  [1mIn [38;5;153mapp.js[0m, two changes. On load, prefill [38;5;153m#username[39m from [38;5;153mrememberedUsername[39m when it's non-empty. On login, save the
  username — gated on [38;5;153mresult.success[39m, so it behaves correctly once [38;5;153mlogin()[39m stops being a stub that always returns true.

  [1mThe password is never persisted, under any preference.[0m There's no schema entry for it and no code path that could add
  one by accident. Worth stating explicitly in the spec so nobody later reads "remember the login" as an invitation.

  One thing I want to flag rather than decide for you. A remembered username with no way to turn it off is a genuine
  problem on a shared machine — the next person at that keyboard sees the previous user's name prefilled, and there's no
  UI to clear it. The fix is a "Remember me" checkbox next to the submit button, backed by a second schema entry
  ([38;5;153mrememberUsername[39m, boolean, default true or false); unchecking it clears the stored username. It's maybe fifteen extra
  lines across the markup and the wiring. Strictly it's beyond the v1 scope you picked, which is why I'm asking instead
  of adding it.
